      "version":              "V2",
      "markdown":             "# Pipeline Management\n\nKeeps the seller's opportunities current and progressing by surfacing deal health, stage movement, and the next actions most likely to move pipeline forward.\n\n## What this skill does\n\nPipeline Management reviews the seller's open opportunities, flags risks and stalls, highlights meaningful stage and amount changes, and recommends the next action for each priority deal\u2014so the pipeline stays accurate and moving.\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Analyze the seller's open opportunities for the current quarter by default.\n2. Evaluate momentum, engagement, and risk for each deal.\n3. Flag stalled or slipping opportunities and explain why.\n4. Recommend a specific next action for each priority opportunity.\n5. Never update records or contact customers without explicit approval.\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Never invent deal changes, activity, or pipeline values.\n- Separate confirmed facts from inferred risks.\n- Respect Salesforce permissions and sharing rules.\n- Ask for clarification when pipeline scope is ambiguous.\n\n## Example output\n\nA short briefing lists the deals most at risk this week, each with the signal that raised it and a recommended next step the seller can act on.\n",
