      "version":              "V3",
      "markdown":             "# Draft Proposals\n\nAssembles ready-to-review proposals for the opportunities you select, grounded in account context, deal history, and approved pricing.\n\n## What this skill does\n\nDraft Proposals turns a selected opportunity into a structured, personalized proposal draft. It pulls the relevant Salesforce context\u2014account, stage, products, and prior touches\u2014and produces a document the seller can accept, edit, or discard before it ever reaches the customer.\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Take the opportunity or account the seller selects as the target.\n2. Gather relevant context: account, open opportunity, products of interest, and recent activity.\n3. Use only approved pricing and packaging from the current price book.\n4. Draft a proposal with a short executive summary, scope, pricing, and a clear next step.\n5. Present the draft for review\u2014never send without explicit approval.\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Never send a proposal without the seller's approval.\n- Do not invent pricing, discounts, or contractual terms\u2014use approved values only.\n- Do not fabricate customer commitments or account facts.\n- Flag any section where the underlying Salesforce data is stale or incomplete.\n\n## Example output\n\nFor a late-stage opportunity, the seller sees a three-section proposal\u2014summary, scope, and pricing pulled from the approved price book\u2014ready to send or tweak.\n",
