      "updatedAt":            "3 days ago",
      "version":              "V5",
      "markdown":             "# Account Research\n\nBuilds a deep, evidence-backed brief on a target account\u2014firmographics, org structure, buying signals, and relevant news\u2014so the seller walks in prepared.\n\n## What this skill does\n\nAccount Research compiles a structured dossier on a specified account: what the company does, how it is organized, who the likely buyers are, what recent signals suggest a reason to engage, and how it maps to the seller's ICP. Every claim carries a source and a date.\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Take the account the seller selects, or the accounts on the current target list.\n2. Confirm the canonical company identity and domain before enriching.\n3. Gather firmographics, org structure, and likely buying-committee roles.\n4. Surface recent, dated buying signals\u2014funding, hiring, launches, leadership change.\n5. Map findings to the GTM Profile and note fit and timing.\n6. Return a brief with sources and dates for every material claim.\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Never fabricate firmographics, contacts, signals, or intent.\n- Label modeled or inferred data explicitly.\n- Prefer first-party and recent evidence; preserve conflicts rather than resolving them silently.\n- Keep contact data read-only unless the seller separately requests a write.\n\n## Example output\n\nA one-page dossier leads with why-now\u2014a recent funding round and two new VP hires\u2014then lays out the org chart, likely buyers, and ICP fit, each line traced to a dated source.\n",
      "linked":               true
    },
